---
layout: page.liquid
title: Guido
description: Your race engineer, on your phone. Guido turns a spare phone or tablet into a live race dashboard and a voice co-driver for sim racing. It speaks Gran Turismo 7 today, with more sims on the roadmap — local, private, and zero-setup.
image: /assets/products/guido/logo-wordmark.png
image_width: 1200
image_height: 1200
screens:
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-dashboard.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-dashboard-thumb.png
    label: Dashboard
    caption: Full-screen landscape dashboard with shift lights, tire temps and gear cues
    alt: Guido dashboard with a 16-LED rev bar, tire temperatures, speed and gear
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-speaking.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-speaking-thumb.png
    label: Voice
    caption: Ask out loud — Guido answers while you keep both hands on the wheel
    alt: Guido dashboard with the voice badge showing green level bars while it answers
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-welcome.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-welcome-thumb.png
    label: Zero setup
    caption: Zero setup — Guido finds your sim on the network by itself
    alt: Guido welcome screen searching the local network for a sim session
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-unlock-pro.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-unlock-pro-thumb.png
    label: Unlock Pro
    caption: Sign in to unlock hands-free voice activation
    alt: Unlock Guido Pro sign-in screen with an email field and the Pro benefits
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-settings.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-settings-thumb.png
    label: Settings
    caption: Your units, your network, your call
    alt: Guido settings with units, connection, account and about sections
  - src: /assets/products/guido/screen-no-signal.png
    thumb: /assets/products/guido/screen-no-signal-thumb.png
    label: Reconnect
    caption: If the stream drops, Guido says so and reconnects on its own
    alt: Guido dashboard showing the no-signal state
---
<a class="product-banner" href="/writing/meet-guido/">
  <span class="product-banner__label">New</span>
  <span class="product-banner__text">Read the launch post</span>
  <span class="product-banner__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{ 'arrow-right' | lucide }}</span>
</a>

<section class="product-hero">
  <div class="product-hero-content">
    <div class="product-hero-logo-tile">
      <img
        src="/assets/products/guido/logo.png"
        alt="Guido logo"
        width="640"
        height="640"
        eleventy:ignore
        loading="eager"
        decoding="sync"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    </div>
    <h1 class="product-hero-title product-hero-title--guido">Guido</h1>
    <p class="product-hero-tagline">Your personal race engineer for sim racing</p>
    {% assign waitlist_product_id = 'bed09cd5-2e0d-43b7-ace6-cdf9e8fc3dbc' %}
    {% assign waitlist_heading = null %}
    {% assign waitlist_note = "Closed beta on Android. We'll email your invite when there's room." %}
    {% include 'waitlist-form.liquid' %}
  </div>
  <a class="product-hero-scroll" href="#screens" aria-label="See the dashboard and what Guido does">
    {{ 'arrow-down' | lucide }}
  </a>
</section>

<section
  class="product-screens"
  id="screens"
  x-data="{ index: 0, count: {{ screens | size }}, prev() { this.index = (this.index - 1 + this.count) % this.count }, next() { this.index = (this.index + 1) % this.count } }"
>
  <h2 class="product-section-title">Built for the track, not the pit lane</h2>
  <div class="guido-gallery">
    <div
      class="guido-gallery__stage"
      tabindex="0"
      role="region"
      aria-roledescription="carousel"
      aria-label="Guido screenshots"
      @keydown.arrow-left="prev()"
      @keydown.arrow-right="next()"
    >
      {% for shot in screens %}
        <figure
          class="guido-gallery__slide"
          :hidden="index !== {{ forloop.index0 }}"
          {% unless forloop.first %}
            hidden
          {% endunless %}
        >
          <img
            src="{{ shot.src }}"
            alt="{{ shot.alt }}"
            width="1920"
            height="1080"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          >
          <figcaption class="guido-gallery__caption">
            <span class="guido-gallery__label">{{ shot.label }}</span>
            <span>{{ shot.caption }}</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      {% endfor %}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="guido-gallery__nav guido-gallery__nav--prev"
        @click="prev()"
        aria-label="Previous screenshot"
      >
        {{ 'chevron-left' | lucide }}
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="guido-gallery__nav guido-gallery__nav--next"
        @click="next()"
        aria-label="Next screenshot"
      >
        {{ 'chevron-right' | lucide }}
      </button>
      <span
        class="guido-gallery__counter"
        aria-hidden="true"
        x-text="String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0') + ' / ' + String(count).padStart(2, '0')"
        >01 / {{ screens | size -}}
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="guido-gallery__thumbs">
      {% for shot in screens %}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="guido-gallery__thumb"
          :class="{ 'is-active': index === {{ forloop.index0 }} }"
          :aria-current="index === {{ forloop.index0 }}"
          @click="index = {{ forloop.index0 }}"
          aria-label="Show {{ shot.label }}"
          title="{{ shot.label }}"
        >
          <img
            src="{{ shot.thumb }}"
            alt=""
            width="512"
            height="288"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          >
          <span class="guido-gallery__thumb-label">{{ shot.label }}</span>
        </button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-features">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">What Guido does</h2>
  <div class="product-features-grid">
    <article class="product-feature-card product-feature-card--primary">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'activity' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">A dashboard built for racing</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        A 16-LED rev bar with shift lights, a big gear and speed readout, per-tire temperature gradients, red downshift
        cues, and live assist status (TCS, ABS, ASM). Landscape, always-on, readable at a glance.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="product-feature-card product-feature-card--primary">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'mic' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">A co-driver you can talk to</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        Hold push-to-talk and ask: how much fuel is left? How many laps to go? What's the race advice? Guido listens and
        answers out loud, in real time, while you keep your eyes on the track.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="product-feature-card">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'fuel' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">Fuel strategy, handled</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        Guido learns how much fuel your car actually burns per lap, predicts how far your tank will stretch, and speaks
        up with a "box this lap" call before you run dry — not after.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="product-feature-card">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'radar' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">Zero setup</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        Launch the app and it scans your network until your sim session shows up — Gran Turismo 7 today. No IP
        addresses, no port forwarding.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="product-feature-card">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'shield-check' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">Private by design</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        Telemetry never leaves your home network, and your voice is transcribed on your device. No cloud, no ads, no
        analytics. Your races belong to you.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="product-feature-card">
      <div class="product-feature-icon">{{ 'radio-tower' | lucide }}</div>
      <h3 class="product-feature-title">Built for the whole stint</h3>
      <p class="product-feature-desc">
        An always-on, edge-to-edge display that won't sleep mid-session, a one-tap reconnect if the stream drops, and
        your units throughout: km/h, mph or m/s, Celsius or Fahrenheit.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-tiers">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">Two ways to race</h2>
  <div class="product-tiers-grid">
    <div class="product-tier">
      <h3 class="product-tier-name">Free</h3>
      <p class="product-tier-price">No account needed</p>
      <p class="product-tier-desc">The full dashboard and a push-to-talk race engineer.</p>
      <ul class="product-tier-list">
        <li>Live race dashboard</li>
        <li>Proactive calls like "box this lap"</li>
        <li>Push-to-talk questions, answered on-device</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="product-tier">
      <h3 class="product-tier-name">Pro</h3>
      <p class="product-tier-price">Unlocked with a free account sign-in</p>
      <p class="product-tier-desc">Everything in Free, for drivers who don't want to reach for a button mid-corner.</p>
      <ul class="product-tier-list">
        <li>Hands-free voice activation</li>
        <li>Just speak — Guido knows when you're talking to it</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-requirements">
  <div class="product-requirements-card">
    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Gran Turismo 7 running on a PS5, with telemetry enabled in the game settings — the sim supported today</li>
      <li>A phone or tablet on the same home network — Android 7.0 or newer works best mounted beside your wheel</li>
      <li>That's it. No cables, no cloud, no account required for the Free tier</li>
      <li>More sims are on the <a href="#roadmap">roadmap</a> — Guido is built for multiple sims</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-roadmap" id="roadmap">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">Roadmap</h2>
  <ol class="product-roadmap-list">
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Today</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Gran Turismo 7, on Android</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        In closed beta on Google Play: the full dashboard, push-to-talk, and the calls Guido makes on his own when the
        fuel math stops working.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Next</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">iPhone</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        The iOS build is in App Store review and ships as soon as the process clears, from the same codebase.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Next sims</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Le Mans Ultimate, then the Assetto Corsa family</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Le Mans Ultimate is the most likely next stop, quite possibly with the Assetto Corsa family (AC, ACC, AC Evo) in
        the same release. F1 and iRacing follow. Guido is built for multiple sims, and the order is open.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">The engineer keeps learning</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Tyres, shifts, strategy</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Tyre and shift intelligence, richer race strategy, and more questions Guido can answer out loud while you drive.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Longer bets</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Desktop and track detection</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        A desktop build and automatic track recognition are on the list. We'd rather ship them well than promise them
        early.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="product-cta">
  <div class="product-cta-content">
    <h2 class="product-cta-title">Strap in. Guido will watch the numbers.</h2>
    <p class="product-cta-desc">Join the waiting list and we'll send your invite as soon as there's room.</p>
    {% assign waitlist_heading = null %}
    {% assign waitlist_note = 'Already in the closed beta? <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=club.matto.guido">Open Guido on Google Play</a>.' %}
    {% include 'waitlist-form.liquid' %}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="product-tos-link">
  <a href="/products/guido/privacy/">Privacy policy</a>
  ·
  <a href="/products/guido/account-deletion/">Account deletion</a>
  ·
  <a href="/products/guido/terms/">Terms of service</a>
</div>
